    "explanation": "Both of you were at the Tampines interchange private-hire bay, and the platform's own telemetry shows it: the driver's trace holds 25 qualifying fixes inside the 150 m hub arrival radius (closing to 30 m of the pin), and the rider's 88 fixes sit 50-91 m from the same pin, stationary, from 07:43. The $6.00 fee nonetheless does not stand, and the reversal being disputed, driver, was correct.\n\nTHE FEE. The charge depends on POL-NS-01, whose limb (c) requires the driver to hold position inside the pickup geofence for at least 300 seconds for a TRANSPORT_HUB pickup, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. EV-GPS-00209 records a single continuous qualifying in-geofence run of 236 seconds, from 07:44:14 to the 07:48:10 cancellation - 64 seconds short of the minimum. The trip record's wait_time_min of 10.1 is real but runs from the 07:38:05 arrival marker, which POL-NS-01(c) expressly excludes, and the first qualifying fix is 369 seconds after that marker. The shortfall cannot be cured by summing intervals: the trace shows run_count 1, so there is no second in-geofence interval, and POL-NS-06(i) summing in any event requires a present and populated traffic_advisory, which is absent (EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0). The fee is therefore refunded in full under POL-NS-06, and POL-NS-06 and POL-NS-07 both state no driver compensation is payable on a shortfall; POL-NS-07's compensation requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which it is not.\n\nDRIVER'S CASE. Your arrival is established on the policy's own test - 25 consecutive qualifying in-radius fixes, far past the three POL-NS-02 requires - and you terminated a genuine RIDER_NO_SHOW, so limbs (a), (b) and (d) hold. The $6.00 is also the right figure: the greater of the $6.00 TRANSPORT_HUB zone fee and the $4.00 RYDE_X tier fee, matching the fare_breakdown line, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect. But limb (c)'s dwell requirement is the one the fee cannot survive, and it fails on your own telemetry, as your own case concedes. The anti-farming bar does not trip (3 no_show_terminations_30d over 88 completed_trips_30d is 3.4%, below both limbs).\n\nRIDER'S CASE. Your track and the unread messages corroborate your account that you were at the bay and saw nothing until afterwards, but under POL-NS-06 the refund turns on the corrected dwell alone and is independent of your presence or of any message from you, so nothing turns on those points.\n\nDISPOSITION. This dispute was filed by the driver, and the fare record already shows the fee refunded to the rider (payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 6.00). The correct outcome is therefore that the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands: the $6.00 is not restored to the driver and no further refund is owed to either party.\n\nEVIDENCE WEIGHT. EV-CHAT-00209 is impaired at weight 0.85 on issue UNREAD_MESSAGE (the driver's two messages and the system arrival notice carry read_at null). That impairment is consistent with the rider's account and does not touch the deciding fact, which is the GPS dwell; the ruling rests on EV-GPS-00209 at weight 1.0, so the finding is unaffected by the discount. No POL-NS-09 trigger applies (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the trace and trip record do not contradict each other on the deciding point, no repeat-counterparty pattern, the anti-farming check does not trip), so the case is decided rather than escalated, and no clause produces a referral."
